{
  "abstract": "Lean formalization of the balanced reserve and matching results in Lemmas 4.11–4.14 of Chen and Shan’s An Asymptotically Sharp Form of the Overfull Conjecture. Signed edge weights realize prescribed margins in dense bipartite graphs. These weights yield sampling probabilities with balanced expected degrees in cyclic directed pairs. Short path deletions restore exact balance in a dense tripartite graph, and a matching theorem packs edge-disjoint perfect matchings across overlapping bipartite graphs.",
